{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1774129296,"nonce":"oLQ5QgIoXAzRRvEpjhFxULHNWHk=","message":"**Naming correction: PTY backend, not channel backend**\n\nThe backend for channel-connected CLI sessions should remain called \"PTY backend\" (not \"channel backend\"). Channels are also used in SDK mode (injected via mcpServers — see 83b498e). The channel MCP is not unique to PTY sessions.\n\nChannel connectivity is a *property* of any session (keyed off `channel_connected_at`), not a backend type. The sub-tab/event-view logic should key off the channel property, not backend_type.\n\n**Gemini critique incorporated:** Instead of adding a new `channel` BackendType, treat channel connectivity as a capability flag on the existing PTY backend. This avoids updating every switch/case in the frontend.\n\n**UI decision:** Channel events should appear as a sub-tab (Terminal | Events) within the session content area, not as a sidebar tab or split pane. Events are sparse, short-form, and represent different information than the terminal (operational state vs conversation). A notification badge on the Events tab handles time-critical events.","files":null}]}